    "id": "i4",
    "kind": "Javadoc",
    "lines": [
     98,
     116
    ],
    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Exercises one of the three timestamp fields (modify, access or create), which all expose an identical set of accessors. The field is supplied through its setters and getters so that this single routine can drive all three without duplicating the assertions. <p> The checks verify, in order, that: a value set as a {@link ZipLong}, a {@link Date} or a {@link FileTime} is reported consistently by every getter; that sub-second milliseconds are truncated; and that clearing the value through any one of the three setters clears every view of it. </p> @param setZipTime setter accepting the time as a {@link ZipLong} (seconds since epoch). @param setJavaTime setter accepting the time as a {@link Date}. @param setFileTime setter accepting the time as a {@link FileTime}. @param getZipTime getter returning the time as a {@link ZipLong}. @param getJavaTime getter returning the time as a {@link Date}. @param getFileTime getter returning the time as a {@link FileTime}. @param isTimePresent predicate reporting whether the corresponding flag bit is set. @param time the expected {@link ZipLong} value (whole seconds). @param timeMillis the same instant expressed in milliseconds since epoch."
   },
   {
